/**
\page page_stfgtcollection StFgtCollection — FGT Collection Documentation

\brief Top-level event container for all Forward GEM Tracker (FGT) data in StEvent.

\section fgt_overview Overview

\ref StFgtCollection is the root-level container that aggregates all Forward GEM Tracker
(FGT) data for a single STAR event.  The FGT comprised six gas-electron-multiplier disc
detectors in the forward region.  Each disc independently records GEM strip signals.
Three levels of reconstruction are represented:

- **Strip** (\ref StFgtStrip) — individual 1D readout channel carrying raw ADC samples
  and calibration flags.
- **Hit** (\ref StFgtHit) — a 1D cluster of adjacent strips formed within one disc.
- **Point** (\ref StFgtPoint) — a 2D reconstructed space-point formed by intersecting
  an X-layer cluster and a Y-layer cluster.

\section fgt_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

All four collection classes derive directly from \c StObject:

\code
StObject
└── StFgtCollection           (top-level event container)
    ├── StFgtStripCollection  (embedded array[kFgtNumDiscs=6])
    ├── StFgtHitCollection    (embedded array[kFgtNumDiscs=6])
    └── StFgtPointCollection  (single embedded instance)
\endcode

\section fgt_containment Containment Model

\code
StFgtCollection
│   mNumTimeBins : size_t          default 7
│
├── mStripCollection[6]  : StFgtStripCollection
│   ├── mDisc              : Short_t
│   ├── mStripVec          : StSPtrVecFgtStrip   (owns StFgtStrip objects)
│   └── mStripElecIdVec    : StPtrVecFgtStrip    (transient, not streamed)
│
├── mHitCollection[6]    : StFgtHitCollection
│   ├── mDisc              : Short_t
│   └── mHitVec            : StSPtrVecFgtHit     (owns StFgtHit objects)
│
└── mPointCollection     : StFgtPointCollection
    └── mPointVec          : StSPtrVecFgtPoint   (owns StFgtPoint objects)
\endcode

The constant \c kFgtNumDiscs = 6 is defined in \c StEnumerations.h.

\section fgt_ownership Object Ownership

- All sub-collections (\ref StFgtStripCollection, \ref StFgtHitCollection,
  \ref StFgtPointCollection) are **stack-allocated** (embedded) inside
  \ref StFgtCollection; callers must not delete them.
- Each sub-collection holds an \c StSPtrVec (smart-pointer vector) that **owns** its
  leaf objects.  The vector's destructor and \c clear() both delete the pointed-to
  objects.
- \ref StFgtStripCollection additionally holds a transient plain-pointer vector
  \c mStripElecIdVec (keyed by electronics ID) for fast lookup.  It is marked \c //!
  and is not written to the persistent store.  It does not own strips.
- \ref StFgtCollection itself is owned by the StEvent framework (St_DataSet /
  StXRefMain); its destructor is a no-op.
- **Do not delete** any pointer returned by getStripCollection(), getHitCollection(),
  getPointCollection(), getStrip(), or any element from the \c StSPtrVec vectors.

\section fgt_datamembers Data Members

\subsection fgt_dm_top StFgtCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StFgtStripCollection[6] | \c mStripCollection | Strip collections, one per disc (0-based) |
| \c StFgtHitCollection[6]   | \c mHitCollection   | Hit collections, one per disc |
| \c StFgtPointCollection    | \c mPointCollection | 2D point collection for all discs |
| \c size_t                  | \c mNumTimeBins     | ADC time bins sampled per strip (default: 7) |

\subsection fgt_dm_strip StFgtStripCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c Short_t             | \c mDisc           | FGT disc index (0–5) |
| \c StSPtrVecFgtStrip   | \c mStripVec       | Persistent, owned strip vector |
| \c StPtrVecFgtStrip    | \c mStripElecIdVec | Transient lookup by electronics ID (not streamed) |

\subsection fgt_dm_hit StFgtHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c Short_t         | \c mDisc   | FGT disc index (0–5) |
| \c StSPtrVecFgtHit | \c mHitVec | Persistent, owned hit vector |

\subsection fgt_dm_point StFgtPointCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecFgtPoint | \c mPointVec | Persistent, owned 2D-point vector |

\section fgt_methods Key Methods

\subsection fgt_meth_top StFgtCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getNumDiscs() const | Returns \c kFgtNumDiscs (6) |
| \c getNumStrips() const | Total strips across all discs |
| \c getNumStrips(unsigned\ short\ disc) const | Strips on one disc |
| \c getNumHits() const | Total hits across all discs |
| \c getNumHits(unsigned\ short\ disc) const | Hits on one disc |
| \c getNumPoints() const | Total 2D points |
| \c getNumTimeBins() const | Number of ADC time bins |
| \c setNumTimeBins(size_t) | Set the number of ADC time bins |
| \c getStripCollection(unsigned\ short) | Strip collection for disc; \c nullptr if out of range |
| \c getHitCollection(unsigned\ short) | Hit collection for disc; \c nullptr if out of range |
| \c getPointCollection() | Pointer to the point collection |
| \c Clear(Option_t*) | Clears all sub-collections (framework callback) |

\subsection fgt_meth_strip StFgtStripCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getStrip(int\ elecId) | Returns or creates the strip for an electronics ID — the only way to add strips |
| \c getStripVec() | Direct access to the persistent strip vector |
| \c sortByGeoId() | Sorts the strip vector by geometry ID |
| \c removeFlagged() | Removes strips with negative geoIds or \c kFgtDeadStrip seed type |
| \c getNumStrips() const | Number of strips |
| \c getDisc() / setDisc() | Get/set disc index |

\subsection fgt_meth_hit StFgtHitCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getHitVec() | Reference to the owned hit vector |
| \c getNumHits() const | Number of hits |
| \c getDisc() / setDisc() | Get/set disc index |

\subsection fgt_meth_point StFgtPointCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getPointVec() | Reference to the owned point vector |
| \c getNumPoints() const | Number of 2D points |

\section fgt_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
// Obtain StFgtCollection from StEvent
StFgtCollection* fgtColl = event->fgtCollection();
if (!fgtColl) return;

// --- Strips ---
for (unsigned short disc = 0; disc < fgtColl->getNumDiscs(); ++disc) {
    const StFgtStripCollection* sc = fgtColl->getStripCollection(disc);
    if (!sc) continue;
    const StSPtrVecFgtStrip& strips = sc->getStripVec();
    for (const StFgtStrip* strip : strips) {
        if (!strip) continue;
        // strip->getGeoId(), strip->getPedSubtractedAdc(), ...
    }
}

// --- Hits ---
for (unsigned short disc = 0; disc < fgtColl->getNumDiscs(); ++disc) {
    const StFgtHitCollection* hc = fgtColl->getHitCollection(disc);
    if (!hc) continue;
    const StSPtrVecFgtHit& hits = hc->getHitVec();
    for (const StFgtHit* hit : hits) {
        if (!hit) continue;
        // hit->charge(), hit->position(), ...
    }
}

// --- 2D Points ---
const StFgtPointCollection* pc = fgtColl->getPointCollection();
if (pc) {
    const StSPtrVecFgtPoint& points = pc->getPointVec();
    for (const StFgtPoint* pt : points) {
        if (!pt) continue;
        // pt->getPositionX(), pt->getPositionY(), ...
    }
}
\endcode

\warning Never call \c push_back() on the vector returned by \c getStripVec().
         Always use \ref StFgtStripCollection::getStrip(int) to insert new strips.

*/
